queues logs. Followers validate term/previous prefix, truncate supplied conflicts and propagate leader commit accounting into their own queue. FSM execution and future completion occur later on the FSM goroutine. Snapshot transfer substitutes a persisted/restored prefix when logs are unavailable.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-dispatch\",\n        \"b-replicate\",\n        \"b-aggregate\",\n        \"b-append\",\n        \"b-application\",\n        \"b-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-match\",\n        \"f-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src-dispatch\",\n        \"src-request-producer\",\n        \"src-replication-retry\",\n        \"src-replication-loop\",\n        \"src-pipeline\",\n        \"src-replication-completion\",\n        \"src-replication-lifetime\",\n        \"src-commitment\",\n        \"src-leader-commit\",\n        \"src-append-consumer\",\n        \"src-fastpath\",\n        \"src-rpc-dispatch\",\n        \"src-apply-consumer\",\n        \"src-fsm-run\",\n        \"src-fsm-contract\",\n        \"src-startup\",\n        \"src-install\",\n        \"src-replication-snapshot\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A2: contact timeout triggers a eligible local voter campaign; pre-vote probes where supported, then electSelf persists a new term/self vote and asks configured voters through a campaign-local response channel. Vote receivers reject ineligible/stale or less-up-to-date candidates and preserve one vote per term. Majority grants install leader state. Higher-term requests, replication higher-term responses, loss of lease quorum and committed removal can end tenure. Transfer first catches up its target then requests an accelerated campaign. Startup restores term, snapshot and membership history but starts as follower.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-election\",\n        \"b-leader-context\",\n        \"b-membership\",\n        \"b-transfer\",\n        \"b-recovery\",\n        \"b-history\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-authority\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src-campaign\",\n        \"src-election-producer\",\n        \"src-vote-handler\",\n        \"src-prevote\",\n        \"src-persist-context\",\n        \"src-follower-loop\",\n        \"src-leader-lifetime\",\n        \"src-replication-lifetime\",\n        \"src-lease\",\n        \"src-leader-commit\",\n        \"src-config-types\",\n        \"src-config-transform\",\n        \"src-config-admission\",\n        \"src-dispatch\",\n        \"src-config-consume\",\n        \"src-startup\",\n        \"src-install\",\n        \"src-replication-snapshot\",\n        \"src-snapshot-create\",\n        \"src-transfer\",\n        \"src-timeout-now\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Each tenure creates fresh commitment/replication objects, captures its term and sends a no-op; the current-term threshold constrains commitment of inherited history. Old RPC replies retain old campaign channels or commitment pointers, while follower term checks reject obsolete requests. Leader exit signals replication to stop and fails pending client/verify futures; it does not erase stored or already queued history. New authority is constrained by log freshness and recovered configuration. Configuration changes serialize after a current-term commit, then alter voter eligibility while retaining matching support for retained voters. Committed entries are separately consumed by the FSM, and a failed client future does not imply absence from later history. VerifyLeader is another authority consumer whose voter threshold and all-peer notifications have an unresolved eligibility relationship.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-election\",\n        \"b-leader-context\",\n        \"b-membership\",\n        \"b-replicate\",\n        \"b-aggregate\",\n        \"b-application\",\n        \"b-client\",\n        \"b-verify\"\n      ],\n