{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The developer documentation explicitly describes `VerifyLeader` as confirming leadership through heartbeats to voters. Together with its voter-majority threshold and stale-read API purpose, this supports a focused obligation: nonvoter replies must not contribute to that quorum count. I’ll keep actual stale-read consequences outside this obligation.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); c=r['candidates'][0]; q=c['question']; cid=c['id']\nsources=[dict(id='src-verify-doc',file='docs/README.md',start_line=39,end_line=49,kind='document_statement'),dict(id='src-verify-future-purpose',file='future.go',start_line=236,end_line=245,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='src-verify-existing-tests',file='raft_test.go',start_line=1866,end_line=1972,kind='test_expectation')]\nq['source_ids'] += ['src-verify-doc','src-verify-future-purpose','src-verify-existing-tests']\nq['question']='Does the VerifyLeader support tally exclude a configured nonvoter acknowledgment from the voter quorum used to confirm current leadership?'\nq['unknowns']=['Actual post-registration tally and completion when the only additional positive acknowledgment comes from a configured nonvoter.','A legal producer-to-consumer schedule distinguishing nonvoter support from pending voter callbacks.']\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['preferred_check']='controlled_schedule'\nq['trigger_rationale']='Developer documentation identifies voters as the verification support participants; quorumSize computes their majority. Registration and notification instead cover all replication peers. A bounded local eligibility comparison can observe whether a nonvoter acknowledgment increments that count; it need not infer a global stale read or wait for a numeric progress deadline.'\nclaimid='claim-verify-voter-eligibility'\nexpect=['src-verify-doc','src-verify-contract','src-config-types']\ncode=['src-verify-start','src-verify-vote','src-verify-notify','src-verify-result','src-lease','src-replication-lifetime']\nclaim=dict(id=claimid,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='Within a stable configuration and an active leader verification request, an acknowledgment from a configured Nonvoter must not increase the support count toward the voter quorum used by VerifyLeader to confirm leadership.',source_ids=expect+code,scope=dict(description='Participant eligibility in the per-request VerifyLeader quorum tally, with an unchanged mixed voter/nonvoter configuration and no concurrent leadership/configuration transition during the measured accounting step.',assumptions=['Correct peer identities and suffrage; non-Byzantine, well-formed acknowledgments.','An active verification request with initial self support and a configured voter-majority threshold.'],excluded=['Whether another leader is actually elected.','External stale-read or split-brain consequences.','Membership changes during verification, transport impersonation and restart recovery.','A guarantee that a permitted voter acknowledgment necessarily completes verification.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=code,expectation_ids=expect,binding_ids=['bind-verify-registration','bind-verify-notification','bind-verify-tally'],derivation='src-verify-doc describes verification by heartbeats to voters; src-verify-contract identifies confirmation of leadership as its purpose, including prevention of stale reads. src-config-types distinguishes Voter and Nonvoter roles. The actual threshold is quorumSize, whose src-lease definition counts voters only. Therefore the support count being compared against that threshold must count eligible voters: an arbitrary nonvoter cannot substitute for one of those participants. The code that registers all replication peers and counts notifyAll results is the subject of comparison, not normative authority that weakens this requirement. The requirement is necessary eligibility accounting, not an assertion that a quorum always succeeds or that every excess tally causes an observed stale read.',applicability='Stable mixed-suffrage configuration, locally active leader verification, response identity known independently of its success value.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Independent voter-only lease checking can later demote a leader, but does not change the participant eligibility of this verification tally.','Sending heartbeat messages to nonvoters is not itself forbidden; counting their acknowledgment toward a voter quorum is the checked distinction.']))\nbindings=[]\nfor id,mat,sym,a,b,desc in [('bind-verify-registration','src-verify-start','Raft.verifyLeader',965,988,'Initializes self support and voter quorum threshold, then registers the request with replication peers.'),('bind-verify-notification','src-verify-notify','followerReplication.notifyAll',100,112,'Drains peer-owned pending verification requests and forwards a Boolean acknowledgment.'),('bind-verify-tally','src-verify-vote','verifyFuture.vote',274,295,'Increments per-request support and signals completion at its threshold.')]:\n bindings.append(dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=expect,rationale='This bound implementation step participates in the voter-qualified verification support path described by the obligation.')]))\nm=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='b-verify':\n  b['unknowns']=['Can a nonvoter response increment the voter-threshold tally in an actual post-registration execution with known responder identity?','Which legal timing histories make a false verification success externally stale despite independent lease checks?']\n# No assertion or identity change to f-verify-support; only the responsibility question is now grounded outside the map.\njson.dump(m,open('map-obligation.json','w'),indent=2)\np=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=cid,question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,sources=sources,map_path='map-obligation.json',map_changes={'b-verify':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src-verify-doc','src-verify-contract','src-lease'],rationale='The voter-support responsibility is now grounded in the documentation/API and voter threshold; remove the answered normative unknown, retaining actual execution and wider endpoint questions.',preserves='The Fact remains the observed all-peer counter representation, and all producer/consumer dependencies and eligibility suspicion remain unchanged. No requirement or observation has yet been executed.')},rationale='Ground the selected local participant-eligibility obligation using implementation-specific developer documentation and API purpose. Formal execution will separately establish whether nonvoter acknowledgments affect the count.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[cid,'b-verify','f-verify-support','src-verify-doc','src-verify-existing-tests'],answered='The verification responsibility is grounded locally: docs/README.md names voters as the confirmation participants, while quorumSize computes a voter majority. Existing verification tests cover all-voter success, a single voter, rejection after term change, and partial connectivity; none of the read cases supplies a mixed-suffrage eligibility witness. A nonvoter may recognize the leader but cannot provide one of the voter contributions required by this tally.',remaining=q['unknowns']+['Actual stale-read consequences remain independent of the local eligibility obligation.'],understanding='updated',rationale='An eligibility error can be measured independently of a later endpoint. Lease demotion remains counterevidence against assuming a stale-read consequence; it is not a substitute participant for verification.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=q['unknowns'],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 make_obligation.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-12-06-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
